Z||000000||ur2biteme||10-18-2001||11:33 PM||||well, a few months back my roomate was borrowing my car long-term to get back and forth from work and a few other places, and he comes home one day and tells me that the engine is knocking.  i go outside and check, and sure enough, when i rev it it knocks like a s.o.b.  at idle the knock is present but nowhere near as loud as it is under throttle.  we fired it up a few days later and it was knocking something terrible regardless of RPM.  other than that, it ran just like it did before it developed the knock.  oh, and he told me that he filled the oil (it notoriously dumps oil on the ground, always has)<P>well, the latest on it is i got an idea to try something.  i went and bought some oil and filled it back up (it had been sitting for a few months) and fired it up again.  it knocked like hell until the fast idle calmed down, and when it dropped (about 1400, 1500 rpm) the knock went away almost entirely and stayed that way until i even slightly reved it.  even when it knocked, it didnt knock as bad as it did, but still sounded horrible.  <P>i wanted to say a bearing went out, but i've been wrong too many times about stuff like this and would like some advice if possible. just trying to figure out what needs to be fixed, if the engine can be fixed.  thanks in advance||||reg||5
Z||000001||4BanGinFun||10-19-2001||10:11 PM||||i think its beyond a bearing  it sounds like its time for a rebuild its more then likely that your crank is scared now. you could have a bad lifter or two. as far as the oil leak you need new seals if you had replaced then when it started leakin you may have been able to avoid this problem but sh!t happens.  <p>[This message has been edited by 4BanGinFun (edited 10-19-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||ur2biteme||10-19-2001||10:46 PM||||ya, i knew it was rebuild time (as far as i'm concerned, a bearing is rebuild time). as for the oil leak, i wasnt really concerned about that.  it ran ok, i was more worried about internals.  well, time to get it towed to my "garage".  lol.  thanks for the input||||reg||1
