Z||000006||ur2biteme||10-19-2001||11:47 PM||||i'm looking at the realistic cost of swaping to a 60 degree v6 of sorts.  money is an issue, but not so much an issue that i'm gonna back out if it hits like $300 or something like that. i'm looking for an inexpensive upgrade that'll be REAL easy to smog (a 3.4 can look like a 2.8 to a smog tech, or so i've been told) and is about as cheap as i can get without sacrificing quality or reliability.  i'd be perfectly happy with a low mileage or a rebuilt (by me) 2.8 back there with some mild mods.  i drive delivery right now and my Z gets 13 mpg (but it's a damn nice ride) and i want something better on gas.<P>right now i'm thinking of finding a parts car with a 6, swapping the necessacary parts (i wanna keep my isuzu 5 speed) maybe rebuilding in the process.  i have a fairly new clutch (not even 7000 miles) and time isnt that much of an issue.  i'll probably be doing the work myself.  maybe taking an engine rebuilding class in the spring.  anyway, now that i've wasted bandwith i'm done.  any ideas would help.  thanks||||reg||1
